Package: bootqcc
Title: Parametric Bootstrap Control Charts for Any Distribution
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mohamad Yamen", "Al-Mohamad", , "yamenmohamad@tabrizu.ac.ir", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-1665-7203")),
    person("Ali Akbar", "Hydari", , "heydari@tabrizu.ac.ir", role = "aut"),
    person("Hossein", "Jabbari Khamnei", , "h_jabbari@tabrizu.ac.ir", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Builds Phase I control limits for a quantile (or any user-defined
    statistic) of an arbitrary parametric distribution by parametric bootstrap
    with maximum likelihood estimation, then evaluates the chart through
    Monte Carlo estimates of the average run length (ARL). The distribution can
    be any family with d/q/r functions, whether built into R or defined by the
    user, so the same code serves Weibull, gamma, Kumaraswamy, Lindley-type and
    other lifetime models. Phase II monitoring of new samples is supported.
